-### Rubric versioning
-
-Every save snapshots the rubric automatically (capped at 20 + any manual versions). Open the version history to compare and restore any previous version. Versions are stored separately from the rubric record so they don't bloat sync traffic.
-
-**Graded work keeps its rubric version.** A saved grade keeps the rubric and grade scale it was given with, so later edits never silently change a grade or the letter a student sees. Reopening such a grade shows a banner: *Show changes* lists the differences, and *Regrade on latest version* moves the grade to the current rubric and scale (scores carry over where the criterion and level still exist; nothing changes until you save). To move every grade of a rubric at once, choose *Update grades* when the builder asks after saving a change.
