+# Live Writing Sessions
+
+> A timed, whole-class writing sprint: students join with a code, pick their name, write against a shared timer, then self-check and vote on anonymous texts. No accounts and no AI.
+
+**Access:** Live writing (sidebar) → `/live`. Needs cloud sync (Supabase).
+
+## The loop
+
+1. **Set up** — write a prompt, choose the class, minutes per round, number of rounds (default 1, up to 3), and optional minimum/maximum words. Optionally switch on teacher-written hints, the leaderboard, and *lock joining after start*.
+2. **Open the lobby** — a join page shows a code and QR code for the projector. Students enter the code and choose their own name from the class list (or join from the portal, which skips the name picker).
+3. **Write** — students write in a focus-style editor with the prompt, timer and live word count. The projector shows the timer and progress.
+4. **Reflect** — at time-up the text is handed in automatically. Students self-evaluate (three emoji options) and, if enabled, read two anonymous texts and vote for the better one.
+5. **Finals** — anonymous finalists appear on the projector; the teacher can reveal names.
+
+A session moves through the stages *draft → lobby → writing → voting → finals → closed*.
+
+## Why it fits the classroom
+
+Because students join through the roster, the writing is linked to the real student record and can flow into your normal grading — it is not throwaway text.
+
+## Notes
+
+- A vocabulary-based CEFR estimate is shown as an **early indicator** only. It is never added to CEFR leveling and never graded.
+- The teacher monitor has since gained extras (triage strip, nudge presets, timeline, typed-vs-pasted signals, projector hand-off and session export). They are new, so check the in-app help for the current wording.
+- Draft snapshots are kept 30 days and then removed automatically.
+- Design decisions are recorded in `docs/PHASE_43_LIVE_WRITING_SESSION_PLAN.md` in the repository.
