+# Fill-the-gap with dropdowns
+
+> Choose the missing word from a dropdown in each gap.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+Grammar choices (tenses, prepositions, articles) where typing would add spelling noise.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Write gaps as `{{right|wrong|wrong}}`. Mark correct answers with `=` and wrong options with `~` — you can mark several correct (e.g. "don't" and "do not").
+- Use **Suggest distractors** for plausible wrong options.
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic, per gap. A dropdown gap accepts its first option unless you mark several with `=`. With partial credit on, each gap is one share of the points.
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- Shown options make this a recognition task, easier than typing the word ([Fill-the-gap](Question-Type-Cloze)).
+
+## Open research question
+
+*Recognition (dropdown) vs. production (typed) gaps and what each tells you about a level.* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
