+# Fill-the-gap (cloze)
+
+> Type the missing word into a gap in a passage.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+Grammar and vocabulary in context; FCE/CAE-style open cloze and word formation.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Write gaps as `{{answer}}`, or click the **gap pill** in the rich-text prompt. Alternatives go in the gap separated by `|`.
+- Tick **Word formation** for FCE/CAE Part 3 style, with the stem in brackets: `her {{happiness}}(HAPPY)`.
+- **Generate gaps** can turn a pasted passage into gaps (fixed-ratio / C-test, part-of-speech, above-level vocabulary, academic words). Review before saving.
+- The dropdown variant has its own page: [Fill-the-gap with dropdowns](Question-Type-Cloze-dropdown).
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic, per gap. Typed gaps accept every listed alternative. A dropdown gap accepts its first option unless you mark several with `=`. With partial credit on, each gap is one share of the points.
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- Per-gap results feed item analysis, so you can see which gap was hard.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*Cloze deletion method (rational vs. fixed-ratio vs. C-test) and what each measures.* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
