+# Dictation
+
+> Students type what they hear.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+Listening-to-writing, spelling, sentence-level accuracy.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Write the target sentence. Attach audio, or let the browser voice read it (fine for practice; upload a clip for graded tests).
+- Set a **play limit** if wanted. The limit is enforced in the browser, so it deters rather than prevents replays.
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic, **no speech recognition**. The response is aligned word-by-word to your text (edit distance over words). Score = 1 − (word errors ÷ target words), never below zero. Case and punctuation never count; opt-in tolerances apply.
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- Word-level scoring means one wrong word costs the same whether it is a typo or a wrong word.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*Dictation scoring schemes (word vs. character level, error weighting).* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
