+# Error correction
+
+> Find and fix the errors in a passage.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+Proofreading and editing skills.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Mark fragments as `[[wrong|right]]` for an error or `[[fine]]` for a decoy.
+- Students never receive the corrections — they are stripped before delivery (on Supabase-hosted assignments; offline share-code tests include the key).
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic. One mark for *finding* each error and one for *fixing* it correctly. Optional **penalty** for selecting a fragment that was fine.
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- Decoys (`[[fine]]`) matter: without them students can mark everything.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*Penalising false positives in proofreading tasks.* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
