+# Key word transformation
+
+> Complete a second sentence using a given key word, unchanged.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+FCE/CAE Part 4 style grammar and lexical transformation.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Give the first sentence, the key word and the start of the second sentence.
+- Write accepted answers as `part one//part two` — each `//` part is one mark.
+- Set the **word limit** (default 2–5, key word included).
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic. Each part is found as a contiguous run of words in the answer; part two must come after part one. An answer outside the word limit, or one that changes the key word, earns nothing. Each part earns an equal share.
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- A correct answer phrased differently from your accepted list scores zero — add alternatives, or check near-misses in the grading queue.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*How many accepted variants are needed before auto-marking is fair.* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
