+# Matching
+
+> Pair items from two lists.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+Vocabulary–definition, word–picture, cause–effect.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Add the pairs. Pairs can be shuffled per student.
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic; each correctly matched pair is a share of the points (partial credit supported).
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- Unequal list lengths (extra distractors on one side) reduce guessing.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*Guessing rates in matching items.* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
