+# Multiple-choice
+
+> Pick the one correct option.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+Quick checks of reading/listening comprehension, vocabulary and grammar recognition.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Add options and tick the single correct one.
+- Options can carry an **image**, or **audio** (for minimal pairs / "which sound").
+- Use **Suggest distractors** to get plausible wrong options (other word forms, common confusables, same-level words).
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic. Full points for the correct option, zero otherwise.
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- Recognition is easier than production — a B1 student can often *recognise* a form they cannot yet *produce*.
+- With 4 options, blind guessing gets 25%. Consider this when setting a pass mark.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*Guessing correction and how option count affects reliability.* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
