+# Multiple-response
+
+> "Select all that apply."
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+Questions with more than one right answer, e.g. "Which of these are irregular verbs?"
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Add options and tick every correct one.
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic. With partial credit on (the default), the score is the share of options the student got *right in either direction* — correctly ticked **and** correctly left blank. With it off, only an exact match scores.
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- Because correctly *leaving out* a wrong option earns credit, a student who ticks nothing still scores on the options that were meant to stay empty. If that is not what you want, switch partial credit off.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*Whether partial-credit rules for select-all items reward or distort knowledge (see the Research Agenda).* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
