+# Sentence builder
+
+> Rebuild a sentence from shuffled word tiles.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+A1–A2 word order.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Write the target sentence. Use square brackets to keep a phrase on one tile: `She [has been] waiting.`
+- Add alternative accepted orders if several are fine.
+- Choose all-or-nothing or longest-correct-run scoring.
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic. All-or-nothing, or the share of the longest run of words in the right order (best accepted order wins).
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- A sentence only partly in order is flagged for a human, not confirmed automatically.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*Partial-credit schemes for word order.* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
