+# Short-answer
+
+> A word or short phrase typed by the student.
+
+[← All question types](Question-Types) · [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice)
+
+## Best for
+
+Vocabulary recall, spelling, one-word answers.
+
+## How to build it
+
+- Enter the expected answer. Add **alternative answers** separated by `|` (e.g. `colour|color`).
+- Optionally turn on **tolerant matching** (see below).
+
+## How it is scored
+
+Automatic. Case, leading/trailing spaces and repeated spaces are ignored. Opt-in tolerances: ignore punctuation and curly quotes, treat contractions as equal (*don't* = *do not*), accept British/American spelling, accept a one-letter slip in words of 5+ letters. The same rules run in the browser and on the server.
+
+## Watch out for
+
+- A near-miss that fails the match is not marked right automatically; in the grading queue it is flagged for a human to look at.
+- You can adopt a student's answer into the answer key in one click — identical answers from other students are then marked correct too.
+
+## Open research question
+
+*How lenient to be with spelling when the target is meaning versus accuracy.* — tracked in the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda).
