+# Question types
+
+Rubric Maker has 19 question types. Pick one to see what it is for, how to build it and exactly how it is scored.
+
+Every type has an in-app **?** help button too. Auto-scoring runs the same code in the browser and on the server.
+
+## Choose an answer
+
+| Type | What it is |
+|---|---|
+| [Multiple-choice](Question-Type-Multiple-choice) | Pick the one correct option. |
+| [Multiple-response](Question-Type-Multiple-response) | "Select all that apply." |
+| [True / False](Question-Type-True-False) | Decide whether a statement is true or false. |
+| [Fill-the-gap with dropdowns](Question-Type-Cloze-dropdown) | Choose the missing word from a dropdown in each gap. |
+| [Grid (matrix)](Question-Type-Matrix) | Several statements that share the same answer columns. |
+| [Hot text](Question-Type-Hot-text) | Click the right fragments inside a passage. |
+
+## Type or record an answer
+
+| Type | What it is |
+|---|---|
+| [Short-answer](Question-Type-Short-answer) | A word or short phrase typed by the student. |
+| [Open (essay)](Question-Type-Open) | A free-text answer that you grade yourself. |
+| [Fill-the-gap (cloze)](Question-Type-Cloze) | Type the missing word into a gap in a passage. |
+| [Word-bank fill-in](Question-Type-Cloze-bank) | Drag word or sentence tiles from a bank into gaps. |
+| [Dictation](Question-Type-Dictation) | Students type what they hear. |
+| [Key word transformation](Question-Type-Key-word-transformation) | Complete a second sentence using a given key word, unchanged. |
+| [Error correction](Question-Type-Error-correction) | Find and fix the errors in a passage. |
+| [Numeric](Question-Type-Numeric) | A number typed by the student. |
+| [Audio-response](Question-Type-Audio-response) | Students record a spoken answer in the browser. |
+
+## Sort, match or order
+
+| Type | What it is |
+|---|---|
+| [Sentence builder](Question-Type-Sentence-builder) | Rebuild a sentence from shuffled word tiles. |
+| [Matching](Question-Type-Matching) | Pair items from two lists. |
+| [Ordering](Question-Type-Ordering) | Drag items into the right sequence. |
+| [Categorize](Question-Type-Categorize) | Sort items into categories. |
+
+## Scored by hand
+
+**Open** and **Audio-response** are always graded by a teacher (optionally with a rubric). Everything else is auto-scored, and you can override any score.
+
+## Related
+
+- [Tests & Practice](Tests-and-Practice) — modes, assigning, results, live monitor
+- [Placement testing](Placement-Testing) — how adaptive tests choose questions
+- [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda) — open questions about scoring and validity
