+# Sharing & Co-teaching
+
+> Needs cloud sync (Supabase) and, for school-wide options, a school set up by an admin.
+
+## Four ways to share
+
+| Way | What colleagues get | Live or copy? |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Material sharing** | A rubric, test or whole **folder**, view-only or editable | **Live** |
+| **Co-teaching a class** | The class, its grades and test results, plus the rubrics and tests it uses | **Live** |
+| **Marketplace** | Browse, clone and upvote published rubrics, tests, decks and bank items | **Copy** (a snapshot) |
+| **Second marking** | One graded submission sent for an independent mark | Per submission |
+
+## Material sharing
+
+Each rubric, test or folder has a **visibility**:
+
+- **Private** — only you
+- **My co-teachers** — teachers you share a class with
+- **My school** — every teacher in your school, plus your co-teachers
+
+…and an **access** level: *view* or *edit*. A folder's setting applies to everything inside it unless an item overrides it, and you can set a default for new material. Students never get access to shared tests (they hold answer keys). Only the owner can change the sharing or move the item.
+
+## Co-teaching a class
+
+Students page → the class's options menu → **Share with co-teachers…** → add a colleague by email:
+
+- **Can view** — sees the class, its students, grades and test results.
+- **Can view & grade** — also changes any grade or test result in that class (including yours) and can assign your tests to it. Results stay yours, and the grade shows who last changed it.
+- The student list itself stays with the owner: co-teachers see it read-only.
+
+## Marketplace
+
+Publish a rubric, test, flashcard deck or question-bank item for colleagues at your school to clone. It is a snapshot — later edits to your original don't reach copies.
+
+## Good to know
+
+- Comment-bank items can still be shared with the whole school with a single toggle.
+- Sharing changes are written to the admin audit log.
