 ### Question types
 
-| Type | Notes |
+There are **19 question types**. Each has its own article with how to build it and exactly how it is scored — see **[Question types](Question-Types)**.
+
+| Group | Types |
 |---|---|
-| Multiple-choice | One correct option; options can carry images |
-| Multiple-response | "Select all that apply" |
-| True / False | — |
-| Short-answer | Auto-scored, case-insensitive; supports **alternative answers** (pipe-separated list) |
-| Open (essay) | Graded manually |
-| Fill-the-gap (cloze) | `{{gap}}` syntax or the click-to-insert **gap pill** in the rich-text prompt; a dropdown variant offers options per gap. Tick **Word formation** for FCE/CAE Part 3 style gaps with the stem in brackets, e.g. `her {{happiness}}(HAPPY)` |
-| Word-bank fill-in | Students drag (or select-then-click, keyboard-friendly) word or sentence tiles into the gaps; extra distractor tiles, each tile used once by default. Suits A1–B1 word boxes and FCE Part 6 gapped texts |
-| Grid (matrix) | Several statements sharing answer columns (True / False / Not given, A / B / C, or FCE Part 7 matching); each statement scored separately with partial credit |
-| Dictation | Students type what they hear; scored by word-by-word alignment with your text (no speech recognition), case and punctuation ignored |
-| Key word transformation | FCE/CAE Part 4: complete the second sentence using the key word unchanged, within a word limit (default 2–5) shown live; accepted answers written as `part one//part two`, each part earns half |
-| Error correction | Proofreading: mark fragments as `[[wrong\|right]]` or `[[fine]]`; one mark for finding each error, one for fixing it, optional penalty for wrong picks. Students never receive the corrections |
-| Sentence builder | A1–A2 word order: rebuild a sentence from shuffled word tiles; several orders can be accepted; all-or-nothing or longest-correct-run scoring |
-| Hot text | `[[clickable fragment]]` passages |
-| Matching | Pair items; pairs can be shuffled per student |
-| Ordering | Drag to order; optional images/hints |
-| Categorize | Group items into categories |
-| Numeric | Auto-scored with a **tolerance** range |
-| Audio-response | Student records a spoken answer in the browser (teacher-configurable recording cap); optional **preparation time** with a visible cue card, after which recording starts automatically. Played back and graded manually |
